WEBVTT

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.460
<i>Toward the end of the Spring Prayer,</i>

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.770
<i>Main and her companions were attacked.</i>

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.890
Over half of the people who 
attacked the carriage

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.220
were not farmers from Ehrenfest.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.450
But then who...

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.920
Viscount Gerlach's land 
connects to other domains.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.980
Erecting a God of Darkness 
barrier around the carriage

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.200
would require a decent amount of mana.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.820
Perhaps they are middle-class...

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.170
but there is definitely 
a noble leading this.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:48.730
And you think it's a noble 
from another domain.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.100
There is someone else who carried this out.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.940
I sensed some mana from 
the forest just now!

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.110
Considering Damuel sensed 
mana back there...

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.560
They must be Devouring soldiers.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.400
Devouring... soldiers?!

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.470
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:24.980
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:49.020
<b>Chapter Thirty-One
 The Gift from the Blue-Robed Priest and Going Home</b>

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.960
Welcome back, Lady Main.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.390
Thanks for watching over the place, Gil.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:12.780
I'll get your bath ready immediately.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.810
Thank you, Delia.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.000
Lady Main.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.040
Please let us thank you.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.140
Why are you being so formal?

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.350
If you were to measure the worth of 
farmers and gray-robed priests,

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.880
the ones who would be considered 
more important are the farmers

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:29.640
because of their crops and taxes.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:36.470
And yet, you saved us, Lady Main.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:39.560
We were able to live a bit longer 
because of you, Lady Main.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.320
Thank you kindly.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:49.730
<i>During the Spring Prayer, Nicola and 
Monika got put in the kitchen,</i>

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:54.830
<i>and ended up helping Hugo and Ella, 
which livened up the kitchen a bit.</i>

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:02.080
Head Priest, I'm here because
I am told that you summoned me.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.800
Lord Sylvester.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.710
Have a seat.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.190
All right.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:12.610
Main.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.750
You're going to be my guide.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.420
It'll make it easier to look around.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:22.750
Um... A guide to what, exactly?

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:26.330
First, the orphanage. Next, the workshop.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.750
I'll have to look at the forest 
the orphans go to, as well.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:33.240
Uh...

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.750
<b>Confiscation</b>

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:44.510
<b>Confiscation</b>

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:41.580
How dare you work those orphans 
for your own desires?

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.500
Please just don't go confiscating anything!

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.080
Don't worry, Main.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:50.880
I will also be accompanying you 
to the orphanage and workshop.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:58.080
I knew I'd have to see them one day.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.280
I figured it be messier than this, 
but it's surprisingly clean.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:15.440
Head Priest, Lord Sylvester, 
this is my attendant, Wilma,

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:21.200
who also manages the orphanage and takes 
care of the children who haven't been baptized yet.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.960
Thank you for visiting our humble orphanage.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.560
We are truly honored by your visit.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:32.610
Ah... The attendant who created
 those magnificent drawings.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.680
Continue your good work.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:38.090
Th-Thank you very much...

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:40.610
Main.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.080
What is this?

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.960
Those are game cards called karuta.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.800
You have not told me about those.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:49.310
They are not for sale, so 
I did not report them to you.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:50.950
Is that the truth?

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.150
Yes.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.980
I gave Mister Benno the rights,

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:57.760
but we'd have to draw pictures 
for every single card,

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.450
so they can't be mass-produced.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:00.310
Hm...

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:03.820
Then why did you make them?

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.990
So that my attendants can 
learn the alphabet.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.840
I had a set made for the orphanage 
at the workshop at the same time.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:14.220
Did you also make this so they 
could learn the alphabet?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.370
Yes!

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:18.720
We're trapped indoors during the 
winter with nothing to do,

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:22.800
so I made sure they had books to read, or 
could play games with karuta or playing cards,

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.100
and now they can read and write.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.230
They can even do a little arithmetic.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:33.700
I had read the scriptures so 
that I could make these picture books,

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.850
and thanks to them, I was able to learn the 
names of the gods and the divine instruments.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:37.590
Main.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.990
Yes, Head Priest?

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.620
We can discuss this later.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:59.130
Main, where do you make the toys?

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.550
Toys are made by hand in the winter.

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:05.660
The creation of paper and picture books 
takes top priority at the Main Workshop.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.880
But the toys seem more 
interesting and profitable.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.780
Why prioritize paper and picture books?

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.030
Because I want them.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:19.030
So you're doing whatever you want.

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:22.670
Really? You're going to try to scold 
me about that, Lord Sylvester?

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:30.760
This doesn't change the fact that both 
of you are the causes of my headaches.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:35.050
This is Master Benno from 
the Gilberta Company

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.650
and his dapla apprentices, Leon and Lutz.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:42.510
They are in charge of the items created 
in the Main Workshop and the restaurant.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.420
Please treat them kindly.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.550
Oh? Lift your faces.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:49.020
Thank you.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:06.190
May we be blessed that the Goddess of 
Water, Fruhtrane, guided our meeting

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:08.790
pure and true...

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.540
Master... Benno?

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:15.210
Benno, I'd like to talk to 
you about the restaurant.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:16.420
Come.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.530
As you wish.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:23.880
I wonder what's up with Mister Benno.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:24.600
Main.

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:25.660
Yes?

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:27.770
What is this contraption?

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.760
That is the new printing press!

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:36.940
They take these metal letter 
types and create sentences.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:45.470
Lady Main, it's done.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:46.240
Mhm.

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:50.010
We will now print.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:58.050
We can print many pages at once.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.340
We are currently using this rubbing pad 
to transfer the ink onto the paper,

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:05.220
but with an actual printing press, we'll 
be able to print even more pages at once.

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:06.450
Isn't that amazing?

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:09.230
This will change history...

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:10.450
Huh?

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.240
Main.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:16.090
I now have a mountain 
of questions to ask you,

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:17.480
and things I'd also like to tell you.

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:24.960
<i>Fran should be giving him reports... 
I wonder what he wants.</i>

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:34.380
Mister Benno, what did Lord 
Sylvester say to you?

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.340
Ow! Ow!

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:41.000
This is all your fault!

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.310
Argh... Damn it!

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:46.550
What did I do?

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:52.770
What's certain is that a hell of an 
opportunity just fell in my lap.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.190
I have no idea if it's 
gonna work out, though.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:01.200
I have no idea what's going 
on, but do your best...

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:05.190
Dwat huwrts...

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:08.960
The next day,

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:12.630
Lutz and some others led 
him through the forest.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:17.960
That's a shure!

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:20.010
Amazing, isn't it?

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.690
I hunted it down.

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:24.470
Lord Syl was amazing back there!

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:28.300
Yeah! He managed to hit it in one shot, 
even though it was so far away!

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.900
<i>Lord Syl, eh?</i>

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:33.270
<i>Maybe he likes kids, surprisingly.</i>

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.650
Go ahead and feed that to the orphans.

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:38.530
Yay!

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.330
Thank you kindly.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.680
I hadn't had this much fun in a while.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:47.410
Main.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.590
This is a token of my gratitude.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.810
Thank you kindly.

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:56.660
Is this... a magical item?

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:01.310
It is a type of one, but you won't 
be able to use magic with just this.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:03.670
Then what is it used for?

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:06.680
It'll act as a protective 
charm when you need it.

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:09.060
A protective charm?

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:11.620
Turn around. I'll put it on you.

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:19.080
Have you never received an 
accessory from a man before?

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.500
Move your hair out of the way.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:25.200
I've had someone put a hair 
accessory in my hair before.

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:30.690
There.

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:38.030
Make sure you keep that on 
you at all times. Understand?

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:43.680
If you're ever in trouble, press your 
blood seal upon this black stone.

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.000
If I'm in trouble?

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:47.770
Yes.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:50.320
I promise I'll come save you.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.630
Lord Sylvester...

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.490
Got it?

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:56.060
Ow...

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:57.690
No, you're supposed to go, "Pwee."

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:04.910
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:11.000
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:21.760
With books made from parchment,

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:26.010
in order for a single book to be completed,

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:29.130
it takes the hard work of many 
workshops and artisans.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.290
But that's not the case with your book.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:41.530
The text, pictures, and printing 
can all be done in one workshop.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.630
Once your printing press is complete,

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:51.670
it'll be possible to mass produce 
these books in very little time.

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:56.270
Which means that everyone who 
had earned a living making books

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:58.510
will not be in the same 
situation any longer.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:02.110
And that's why you said 
history would change...

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.910
How did your world change

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.110
once books went into the hands 
of farmers and townspeople?

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.500
There were instances where people
 brought down the ruling class,

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:17.540
and the people started 
their own government.

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:21.590
There were also leaders who 
spread information beneficial

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:24.370
to their agenda in order
 to incite their people.

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:27.010
But...

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:33.040
If you're asking me how things will change or 
how some people may take advantage of this...

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.120
I don't have an answer for you.

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:39.010
It would all depend on how this is used...

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.490
How troublesome that we don't know

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:45.040
how this will turn out because the
 effects will be too far-reaching.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:49.630
We can't expect the same thing that 
happened in my world to happen here.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:54.100
This is a world that can't function 
without nobles who can use magic.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:57.760
It's true that it's possible 
to rule with magic.

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.270
But there's no guarantee 
of how that will play out.

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:06.340
What is certain is the pushback 
from the nobles will be grand.

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:13.020
Do not print for a while.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:15.040
Huh? But why?

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:20.600
Many households that lack wealth
 make a living by copying books.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:26.730
If your printing starts to spread, lesser 
nobles will hold a grudge against you.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:31.920
Are you saying that nobles 
 have a vested interest?

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:36.650
Very well. How long should I wait?

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.190
Until you are adopted by Karstedt.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:49.120
If a commoner were to step into noble 
territory, they would instantly be crushed.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:53.900
But if you were a high-class noble who 
received permission from the lord

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:58.210
to print for the sake of the domain, 
you will not be crushed easily.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.730
So two more years...

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.480
How about it, Main?

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:09.560
Perhaps you should let Karstedt 
adopt you at once.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:10.120
Huh?

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.720
N-No!

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:16.970
Are you unsure about having Karstedt 
as your adoptive father?

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:18.470
Of course not.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:22.380
I think Lord Karstedt 
is a wonderful person.

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:23.830
But...

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:28.120
I'm just now realizing how much 
trouble I've caused my parents

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:31.230
because books were all I had on my mind.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:43.410
You're the one who made me realize that 
I need to treasure my current family.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:47.080
So I want to stay with my 
family as long as possible!

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:52.640
If you are that determined, 
my hands are tied.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:58.610
For the next two years, just make a 
few children's books here and there.

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:01.700
I understand.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.970
By the way, Head Priest.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:10.550
What is your relationship 
with Lord Sylvester?

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:12.600
What do you mean?

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.850
You seem a bit too familiar with...

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:19.240
I mean, you two seem rather close.

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:22.740
It's better that you don't stick 
your nose where it doesn't belong.

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:24.910
I see...

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:27.220
Then if you'll excuse me.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:29.240
I'm not done talking to you yet.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:30.040
Huh?

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:32.890
Contact your family.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:34.310
Huh?

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.090
You may go home.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:41.670
Okay!

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:50.680
Are families that nice to have?

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:53.160
For me, I feel like I belong there.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:55.550
It's where I'm most at ease.

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:56.710
Huh...

00:16:58.070 --> 00:16:59.300
Main!

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:00.660
We came to get you!

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:05.530
Dad! Tuuli!

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:15.250
See you again tomorrow, Lady Main.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.330
Try not to go out alone.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:20.270
Yes, I won't.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:22.510
I'm home, Mom!

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:24.260
Welcome home, Main.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:26.770
Wow, you look like you're 
going to pop any second.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:30.220
The baby is going to be here any day now.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:34.020
They might have been waiting 
for you to get home.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:37.300
Your big sis is home now.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.520
Whoa, they kicked me.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.770
I'll go get the midwife!

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:58.300
I'll go get some water!

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:03.880
Mom, remember. Hee hee hoo. Hee hee hoo...

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:08.980
<i>Once someone is in labor, women 
from around town come to help.</i>

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:14.150
<i>The men pluck and carve chickens, and 
prepare for the naming ceremony.</i>

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.500
<i>That seems to be the custom in this world.</i>

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:22.030
<i>I asked Lutz to tell the church that I wouldn't
 be able to go to the cathedral for a while.</i>

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:32.080
Then I'll report that Lady Main 
was holding a celebration

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:36.260
for someone in the lower part of 
the city who has helped her out.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:38.840
Thanks. Also, if you could...

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.250
I will not tell Delia about this.

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:44.060
A celebration?

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:48.610
Please let them be born 
without any problems.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:51.230
Please be born without a problem this time.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.890
Please just be well—

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:55.730
Dad! Main!

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.360
He's born!

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:05.390
Effa!

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:06.610
Mom!

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:09.340
He's a healthy baby boy.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.370
What's his name? Do you 
have one for him yet?

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:18.230
Yeah. It's Kamil.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.090
Kamil...

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:23.630
Kamil... It's your big sis.

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:34.000
Oh, no! He started crying.

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:36.860
Well, that's what babies do, dear.

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:43.350
<i>I'll only be able to be with Kamil 
for the next two years.</i>

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:47.180
<i>To make sure that Kamil doesn't forget me,</i>

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:50.650
<i>I'm going to make lots and 
lots of picture books.</i>

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:58.070
Sadly, the high priest currently 
isn't here because he was invited

00:19:58.070 --> 00:19:59.890
to visit by a giebe in the south.

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:01.100
I see...

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:05.260
In that case, please tell him that someone 
Lady Main knows in the lower part of the city

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.770
was celebrating something.

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:07.570
I will.

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:13.100
You move much more elegantly now, Delia.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:17.050
I'm just copying Rosina.

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:17.900
I see...

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:20.150
Is Rosina well?

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:24.630
This takes me back to when 
I was serving Lady Christine.

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:29.370
Back then, I would dance every night

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.160
as Rosina played her harspiel.

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:33.790
Then Wilma would draw that.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:37.680
Rosina continues to play 
her harspiel every day.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:43.010
I see. So she is still 
living the same life.

00:20:44.900 --> 00:20:45.840
Jenni?

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:48.720
Oh, I have good news, by the way.

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:50.060
What is it?

00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:53.730
We are going to have a visitor very soon...

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:57.690
And I hear that this noble 
likes little children.

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:01.900
I see. He likes little children...

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:04.460
Make sure you look more presentable.

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:06.160
Thank you, Jenni.

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:12.320
<i>If this noble takes a liking to me and 
I end up as his mistress,</i>

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:14.610
<i>I might be able to leave the cathedral.</i>

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:17.660
That noble...

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:20.130
Doesn't like normal children...

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:23.160
He's apparently looking for 
a child with the Devouring.

00:22:56.980 --> 00:22:59.980
<b>Next Chapter
The Abandoned Child of the Cathedral and Making Colors</b>

00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:01.520
Hey, Dad.

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:02.750
What is it, Main?

00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:06.030
You said, "Please be born without 
a problem this time," right?

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:07.520
What did you mean by that?

00:23:07.520 --> 00:23:10.220
Ah... Well, our first child miscarried.

00:23:10.220 --> 00:23:10.670
Huh?

00:23:10.670 --> 00:23:13.960
The boy we had next died 
within a year of his birth.

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:16.660
You and Tuuli made it just fine,

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:19.250
but our next child didn't 
survive the winter, either.

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:20.330
And the one after that...

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:23.570
What?! You mean it was that 
hard to have a baby?!

00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:25.220
We offer thanks to the gods!

00:23:25.220 --> 00:23:30.730
We thank the kindred of the Goddess of 
Water, the Goddess of Childbirth Entrinduge,

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:32.720
for her blessing and protection.

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:34.430
For her blessing and protection!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.010
Illustration by: Karasuba Ame
